  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "• Boil the kettle. Half-fill a medium saucepan with boiling water.\n• Cook udon noodles over medium-high heat, gently stirring with a fork to separate, until tender, 1-2 minutes.\n• Drain, rinse and set aside.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/67d7d9c418d6e477003fc8a7/step-835e6900.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• Meanwhile, roughly chop Asian greens. Slice lime into wedges.\n• Cut firm tofu into 2cm chunks.\n• In a large frying pan, heat a generous drizzle of olive oil over medium-high heat.\n• When the oil is hot, cook tofu and trimmed green beans, turning occasionally, until browned, 5-6 minutes.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/67d7d9c418d6e477003fc8a7/step-8fb99510.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• Add ginger lemongrass paste and satay seasoning and cook until fragrant, 1 minute.\n• Stir in Asian greens, coconut milk, plant-based fish sauce, the soy sauce and a splash of water. Simmer until slightly reduced, 1-2 minutes.\n• Gently stir in cooked udon noodles, baby spinach leaves and a good squeeze of lime juice, until combined, 1 minute. Season to taste.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/67d7d9c418d6e477003fc8a7/step-3e454820.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• Divide satay tofu and coconut curried noodles between bowls.\n• Serve with any remaining lime wedges. Enjoy!",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/67d7d9c418d6e477003fc8a7/step-e3dd5530.jpg"
    }
  ]
}
